#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Run a named job on Colab: sync in, execute detached, poll,
pull results, stop the session on every exit path.

Usage: colab-run <job-name> [--resume RUN_ID] [--caller TAG] [--seed] [--detach] [--session NAME] [-- <job args>...]
       colab-run --poll RUN_ID | --wait RUN_ID [--max SECONDS] | --sweep
       colab-run plant-git-identity --session NAME --repo ID_OR_PATH --tree SESSION_TREE [--caller TAG]
plant-git-identity sets the source repo's configured git
identity (its repo-local user.name/user.email) repo-locally in
a session tree formed outside the seed path, reads it back,
and records the plant on its own run record — beside the key
plant, so a session-side commit carries the repo's identity,
never the forming shell's inheritance. Seeded trees are
planted by the seed itself (the record's bundle_seed entry).
--session NAME (or $COLAB_RUN_SESSION) pins the run to the named
lease: it adopts that session or fails pin-unavailable — never a
silent substitution. A launch is confirmed against the venue:
when the channel answers and no job footprint exists, the run
closes as failed with launch_lost set instead of claiming a run
that does not exist.
Job manifest: jobs/<name>/job.json (JSON: repo code parses it, so not YAML).
--caller TAG (or the manifest's "caller" key, or $COLAB_CALLER)
attributes the run to its thread: it rides the lease acquire and
is stamped on the run record.
--detach launches exactly as the foreground form and returns at
once with {run_id, session, state}: the run's record then advances
only when something reconciles it — --poll (one bounded reconcile:
reader exec + pull + record update; exit 0 complete, 1 failed or
orphaned, 3 still running), a later launch's --resume, or --sweep.
--wait polls the LOCAL record only (zero channel use) until the
run is terminal or --max seconds pass (exit 0 complete, 1 failed
or orphaned, 3 still running at the bound). --sweep reconciles
every non-terminal record against the live list. A launched run's
terminal transition appends exactly one run-terminal event to
var/ui-outbox.jsonl.
The CLI funnel — resolution ($COLAB_BIN, else the uv tool venv,
else PATH, else ~/.local/bin/colab), the NO_PROXY environment, and
the guarded invocation — lives in sync/cli.py, the one module every
consumer loads. This module re-exports its colab / colab_bin /
colab_env / TOKEN under their existing names.

Thin entry: the implementation lives in the sync/runner/ package
(foundation, records, reader, pull, sweep, launch, verbs, main)
and is re-exported here name-for-name from the package's __all__,
because consumers load this module by path and address its
helpers (cr.colab, load_run_record, TERMINAL_STATES, ...).
"""

import sys
from pathlib import Path

sys.path.insert(0, str(Path(__file__).resolve().parent))
import _load  # noqa: E402

runner = _load.sync("runner")
for _name in runner.__all__:
    globals()[_name] = getattr(runner, _name)
del _name

if __name__ == "__main__":
    raise SystemExit(main())
